('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003',
'Versace Mansion (Casa Casuarina)',
'South Beach',
'Old Money',
'Gianni Versace bought this 1930 Mediterranean Revival mansion in 1992 and spent four years turning it into one of the most opulent private residences in the world. The gold-leaf mosaic pool — 24-carat, hand-laid — is the centrepiece. Now operating as Villa Casa Casuarina hotel and restaurant, it remains the most maximally committed address in Miami. Sunday brunch on the pool terrace is an exercise in controlled excess. Dress like you understand what you''re standing in.',
