('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003',
'Fontainebleau Miami Beach',
'Mid-Beach',
'Hotel Lobby',
'Morris Lapidus''s 1954 masterpiece invented the Miami Beach hotel as a spectacle. The sweeping curved facade, the staircase to nowhere, the iconic Lapis nightclub — the Fontainebleau has hosted Sinatra, JFK, and every significant Miami moment in between. After a billion-dollar renovation it''s once again the grandest address on Collins. The lobby alone is worth the visit. The pool situation is a world unto itself.',
