('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003',
'The Biltmore Hotel',
'Coral Gables',
'Old Money',
'John Merrick built the Biltmore in 1926 to anchor his vision of Coral Gables as America''s most beautiful city. The tower was modelled on the Giralda in Seville. Al Capone kept a suite. The pool — at its completion the largest in the world — still draws the city''s establishment for Sunday tea and the annual polo season. The Biltmore operates at a register of wealth that predates the Ocean Drive era by fifty years.',
