('11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003',
'Four Seasons Surf Club',
'Surfside',
'Weekend Aristocrat',
'The original Surf Club was the most exclusive address in 1930s Miami — Frank Sinatra, Winston Churchill, and the Duke and Duchess of Windsor were regulars. The Four Seasons restoration by Thierry Despont kept the original Spanish Colonial cabanas and amplified everything else. Thomas Keller''s restaurant is a separate landmark. The beach club, the pool, the discretion — this is old money''s answer to the South Beach hotel.',
